        "title": "What already matches",
        "body": "- **Back remembers where you were.** The workspace keeps a history of stops, and each stop is a graph, a node and a camera position. Back restores all three.\n- **Going through opens beside,** for an account with the workspace. The graph you left stays open as its own tile.\n- **Opening a graph that is already open lands on it.** It does not get a second copy.\n- **A Portal has a control in its title bar** that opens its graph beside this one. That is the way through the scheme asks for when editing.\n- **A pinned thing pans when dragged by its body,** and moves by its title bar.\n- **A drag never navigates,** and a click never moves anything.\n- **Step out exists,** from a graph to the workspace.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "navigation-today"
        }
      },
