        },
        "title": "A build order",
        "body": "Each step can be seen working before the next begins.\n\n- **1. The node ladder.** Come to it, focus at reading size, inside. Everything else in the scheme leans on focus meaning a distance as well as a place.\n- **2. The tile ladder, and stepping out.** A click frames, then enters. Step out goes one level at a time. Escape steps out.\n- **3. One history, and the trail.** The address bar and the workspace share one Back. An account without the workspace gets the same history for its single slot, so that Back returns it to the end of the connection it left. The trail is drawn from it.\n- **4. Going through.** A Portal’s third click, links, Ctrl-click to open beside without travelling, and double-click as the end of the line.\n- **5. Travel along edges.** Trunks, handles, border ports, and edges inside a graph.\n- **6. Walking.** The arrow keys.\n- **7. Take the ways back out of the graphs.**",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "navigation-today"
        }
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
